# Fixed-width element rejects an out-of-range value

Verifies an `int64[]` element assignment rejects a literal that does not fit
the declared integer width instead of widening the element.

>>> source
let values: int64[] = [1]
values[0] = 999999999999999999999999999999

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `999999999999999999999999999999` for type `int64`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 38, end: 68 }

<<< exit
1
